177
00:14:05,467 --> 00:14:11,629
[SPEAKER_03]: If you're doing that because you're trying to get rid of the thoughts, means you're not even seeing your mind to begin with.

178
00:14:12,530 --> 00:14:17,572
[SPEAKER_03]: You're blaming the thoughts for the problem and then trying to get rid of them by, you know, sensuality, thinker, subha.

179
00:14:18,782 --> 00:14:20,983
[SPEAKER_03]: Hatred, think, love, or something.

180
00:14:21,764 --> 00:14:22,784
[SPEAKER_03]: You're not in your mind.

181
00:14:23,004 --> 00:14:24,945
[SPEAKER_03]: You're doing it because you're blaming the thoughts.

182
00:14:25,786 --> 00:14:28,527
[SPEAKER_03]: So, first, you have to not try to get rid of the thoughts.

183
00:14:29,707 --> 00:14:32,409
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the first message you give to the pressuring dog.

184
00:14:34,630 --> 00:14:34,830
[SPEAKER_03]: No.

185
00:14:35,430 --> 00:14:38,992
[SPEAKER_03]: See, it barks at you, because it also thinks that the thoughts are the problem.

186
00:14:39,592 --> 00:14:41,012
[SPEAKER_03]: Thoughts are scaring the animal.

187
00:14:41,673 --> 00:14:43,434
[SPEAKER_03]: So, the animal is barking at the thoughts.

188
00:14:44,794 --> 00:14:46,395
[SPEAKER_03]: And if you go along with it, well,

189
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:49,102
[SPEAKER_03]: You're affirming what the animal is craving against.

190
00:14:51,864 --> 00:14:56,528
[SPEAKER_03]: So, by conveying the message of no, thoughts are not the problem.

191
00:14:56,728 --> 00:15:02,873
