00:43:23,967 --> 00:43:25,128
[SPEAKER_03]: No.

586
00:43:25,148 --> 00:43:31,053
[SPEAKER_03]: Is there an internal... internally felt fact?

587
00:43:32,705 --> 00:43:33,725
[SPEAKER_03]: Of that seated body.

588
00:43:37,226 --> 00:43:38,846
[SPEAKER_01]: Yeah.

589
00:43:39,266 --> 00:43:40,967
[SPEAKER_01]: There is the fact that I'm sitting.

590
00:43:41,627 --> 00:43:42,947
[SPEAKER_03]: But internally.

591
00:43:43,147 --> 00:43:44,067
[SPEAKER_03]: Internal sense of it.

592
00:43:44,647 --> 00:43:46,288
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, I mean, on the inside.

593
00:43:46,348 --> 00:43:46,808
[SPEAKER_03]: Let's say that.

594
00:43:46,888 --> 00:43:47,528
[SPEAKER_03]: On the inside.

595
00:43:47,968 --> 00:43:48,248
[SPEAKER_01]: Right.

596
00:43:48,328 --> 00:43:50,728
[SPEAKER_01]: But I mean, when that fact that I'm sitting...

597
00:43:51,348 --> 00:43:51,649
[SPEAKER_01]: Sorry?

598
00:43:51,869 --> 00:43:53,569
[SPEAKER_01]: Like, the fact that I'm sitting with all my focus...

599
00:43:53,589 --> 00:43:54,809
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not the fact that you're sitting.

600
00:43:55,849 --> 00:43:59,270
[SPEAKER_03]: It's the internal fact of your sitting.

601
00:44:04,098 --> 00:44:10,580
[SPEAKER_03]: Or, the internal fact that's revealed through recognizing the fact of your external sitting.

602
00:44:10,800 --> 00:44:11,561
[SPEAKER_03]: Let's put it that way.

603
00:44:14,582 --> 00:44:15,242
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you're seated.

604
00:44:15,442 --> 00:44:17,663
[SPEAKER_03]: You cannot possibly doubt that.

605
00:44:17,883 --> 00:44:20,244
[SPEAKER_03]: Maybe you find a different word for it.

606
00:44:20,504 --> 00:44:21,884
[SPEAKER_03]: You could doubt how to express it.

607
00:44:23,305 --> 00:44:24,585
[SPEAKER_03]: But that fact you can't doubt.

608
00:44:27,506 --> 00:44:28,286
[SPEAKER_03]: But how do you know that?

609
00:44:30,167 --> 00:44:32,668
[SPEAKER_03]: Can you tell me you're seated, even if you close your eyes?

610
00:44:34,961 --> 00:44:37,442
[SPEAKER_03]: Even if you're not looking externally at your seated body.

611
00:44:40,263 --> 00:44:41,384
[SPEAKER_03]: So, what are you telling me then?

612
00:44:41,404 --> 00:44:46,526
[SPEAKER_03]: What are you... what are you seeing when you close your eyes and I say, what's your body posture?

613
00:44:47,566 --> 00:44:50,847
[SPEAKER_03]: How do you... Well, let me ask you this.

614
00:44:50,987 --> 00:44:55,629
[SPEAKER_03]: Close your eyes and I'll ask you, do you have a body?

615
00:44:55,649 --> 00:44:56,890
[SPEAKER_03]: Yes.

616
00:44:56,910 --> 00:44:57,590
[SPEAKER_03]: How do you know that?

617
00:44:58,590 --> 00:44:59,851
[SPEAKER_03]: Where did that knowledge come from?

618
00:45:05,835 --> 00:45:06,676
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just there.

619
00:45:07,156 --> 00:45:10,579
[SPEAKER_01]: It's just something that I remember.

620
00:45:12,320 --> 00:45:14,722
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, you remembered it?

621
00:45:15,803 --> 00:45:17,584
[SPEAKER_03]: Where was it before you were remembering it?

622
00:45:18,205 --> 00:45:18,845
[SPEAKER_03]: Was it elsewhere?

623
00:45:23,449 --> 00:45:24,570
[SPEAKER_03]: Can it be elsewhere?

624
00:45:24,970 --> 00:45:27,112
[SPEAKER_03]: Can it be anywhere else but right there?

625
00:45:34,125 --> 00:45:34,365
[SPEAKER_01]: No.

626
00:45:35,086 --> 00:45:35,586
[SPEAKER_03]: Impossible.

627
00:45:36,026 --> 00:45:37,047
[SPEAKER_03]: You can be everywhere else.

628
00:45:37,547 --> 00:45:40,328
[SPEAKER_03]: You can forget about it, distract yourself, go to great extents.

629
00:45:40,948 --> 00:45:43,990
[SPEAKER_03]: But whenever you remember it, you find it where it always was.

630
00:45:45,250 --> 00:45:47,371
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the physicality, the internal side of that.

631
00:45:49,152 --> 00:45:54,255
[SPEAKER_03]: Not your associated images with it, which, of course, are going to follow.

632
00:45:54,275 --> 00:45:56,276
[SPEAKER_03]: When you think of your body, you're going to have images of that.

633
00:45:56,396 --> 00:45:59,857
[SPEAKER_03]: But, as I said, even the general question, do you have a body?

634
00:46:01,758 --> 00:46:02,999
[SPEAKER_00]: You already know the answer to that.

635
00:46:03,966 --> 00:46:07,307
[SPEAKER_03]: So, do I have a body?

636
00:46:07,347 --> 00:46:10,788
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, look at that internal fact of that thing there.

637
00:46:12,128 --> 00:46:19,490
[SPEAKER_03]: What we described in two talks ago, when we lost one, you know, the internal gravity, or whatever you want to call it.

638
00:46:20,430 --> 00:46:21,351
[SPEAKER_03]: There is a physicality.

639
00:46:21,391 --> 00:46:22,411
[SPEAKER_03]: That is the situation.

640
00:46:22,431 --> 00:46:29,873
[SPEAKER_03]: That is the framework for every other subsequent experience you might have on account of your senses.

641
00:46:35,392 --> 00:46:40,136
[SPEAKER_01]: It's kind of the being embodied, so to speak.

642
00:46:40,176 --> 00:46:40,717
[SPEAKER_03]: Sure.

643
00:46:40,737 --> 00:46:41,658
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, you can say that way.

644
00:46:42,899 --> 00:46:51,226
[SPEAKER_03]: So the point of this is that it's not to, like, externally observe your body, but to discern that internal one.

645
00:46:52,507 --> 00:46:55,630
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's the whole satipaṭṭhāna of body within the body.

646
00:46:55,750 --> 00:47:00,414
[SPEAKER_03]: You start thinking the body and find the body, experience the body within your thoughts of that body.

647
00:47:01,230 --> 00:47:08,896
[SPEAKER_03]: And when that becomes your thoughts of the body, experience further internal body in regard to those thoughts of body, to the extent necessary for the final knowledge.

648
00:47:09,036 --> 00:47:17,403
[SPEAKER_01]: I think that's kind of what I was... like, just that... the tendency of kind of getting the idea of, like, oh, it's a mental image... You will.

649
00:47:17,423 --> 00:47:17,943
[SPEAKER_01]: That's how it works.

650
00:47:18,143 --> 00:47:20,946
[SPEAKER_03]: So... Everything has to basically be an image like that.

651
00:47:21,206 --> 00:47:26,570
[SPEAKER_03]: But the point is, through discerning them rightly, you won't take them for granted.

652
00:47:26,770 --> 00:47:27,150
[SPEAKER_03]: That's it.

653
00:47:27,511 --> 00:47:30,213
[SPEAKER_03]: Because there is the factual physicality

654
00:47:32,215 --> 00:47:41,719
[SPEAKER_03]: Always at that same place, so to speak, at that same space, that you are experiencing.

655
00:47:45,140 --> 00:47:52,263
[SPEAKER_03]: So, in that sense, I know it's not obviously accurate, strictly speaking, but yes, you can feel that, as opposed to think it.

656
00:47:52,963 --> 00:47:57,285
[SPEAKER_02]: But, yeah, like you were saying earlier, that feeling is always experience.

657
00:47:58,311 --> 00:47:58,491
[SPEAKER_02]: What?

658
00:47:58,831 --> 00:48:05,515
[SPEAKER_02]: So, yeah, yeah, I'm just basically repeating what I was... what you just said, in the sense that... Ah, that feeling, you mean the body is always experienced?

659
00:48:05,535 --> 00:48:06,296
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, of course, yeah.

660
00:48:06,316 --> 00:48:09,698
[SPEAKER_03]: That experience of that internal body is always there.

661
00:48:09,978 --> 00:48:10,198
[SPEAKER_02]: And...

662
00:48:11,019 --> 00:48:11,939
[SPEAKER_02]: It's just being covered up.

663
00:48:12,139 --> 00:48:14,381
[SPEAKER_02]: Regardless of the mood, regardless of the pressure.

664
00:48:14,461 --> 00:48:15,802
[SPEAKER_02]: Regardless, regardless, regardless.

665
00:48:15,962 --> 00:48:17,623
[SPEAKER_02]: It's the... it's... it's the container.

666
00:48:17,963 --> 00:48:18,703
[SPEAKER_02]: Let's put it that way.

667
00:48:19,184 --> 00:48:19,584
[SPEAKER_03]: So that...

668
00:48:20,144 --> 00:48:25,267
[SPEAKER_03]: It's the basis for all of your, as I said, particular sight, sound, smell, taste, touches, thoughts.

669
00:48:27,229 --> 00:48:27,989
[SPEAKER_02]: That... that would be...

670
00:48:29,277 --> 00:48:36,718
[SPEAKER_02]: Like, taking the pressure, for example, as a sign of the... as the mind, but then, not... that... that...

671
00:48:37,999 --> 00:48:39,079
[SPEAKER_02]: There, we're taking the pressure.

672
00:48:39,099 --> 00:48:40,239
[SPEAKER_02]: Sorry, yes.

673
00:48:40,979 --> 00:48:41,339
[SPEAKER_02]: It's alright.

674
00:48:41,819 --> 00:48:57,362
[SPEAKER_02]: The... the uninterruptedness of feeling, feeling, will be, yeah, less perturbed, the more that, yeah, this practice of... of...

675
00:49:00,455 --> 00:49:10,600
[SPEAKER_03]: Discerning the relationship between physicality of the body and... Well, yeah, but see, like, you're not... you're only discerning the relationship marginally, really.

676
00:49:10,640 --> 00:49:11,800
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not about the relationship.

677
00:49:12,301 --> 00:49:16,723
[SPEAKER_03]: It's not about discerning it in a sense of figuring it out, how it relates.

678
00:49:17,543 --> 00:49:19,144
[SPEAKER_03]: It relates by being there.

679
00:49:19,824 --> 00:49:20,865
[SPEAKER_03]: These two things are there.

680
00:49:20,905 --> 00:49:21,705
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the relationship.

681
00:49:21,725 --> 00:49:29,329
[SPEAKER_03]: So, yes, you do need to discern that, because for as long as you think it relates, it comes from here into there, and then it goes elsewhere, yes, of course.

682
00:49:30,200 --> 00:49:31,120
[SPEAKER_03]: You're not going to see any of it.

683
00:49:31,961 --> 00:49:44,525
[SPEAKER_03]: But if you're recognizing the just mere juxtaposition of the internal physicality and feeling felt, that's the relationship you want.

684
00:49:44,545 --> 00:49:49,586
[SPEAKER_03]: But not... well, of course, discern and then really not cover up.

685
00:49:52,927 --> 00:49:53,748
[SPEAKER_02]: Even if it's neutral.

686
00:49:54,668 --> 00:49:55,068
[SPEAKER_03]: Especially.

687
00:49:55,088 --> 00:49:55,908
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, exactly.

688
00:49:56,969 --> 00:49:57,649
[SPEAKER_03]: That's the whole point.

689
00:49:58,694 --> 00:50:03,055
[SPEAKER_03]: So, yes, you could say there's physicality and there's neither pleasure nor pain felt.

690
00:50:03,395 --> 00:50:03,716
[SPEAKER_00]: Great.

691
00:50:05,136 --> 00:50:08,877
[SPEAKER_03]: So, don't cover up that experience now.

692
00:50:14,699 --> 00:50:16,159
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's, you know, what I was saying before.

693
00:50:16,199 --> 00:50:17,960
[SPEAKER_03]: And then, if you have thoughts, OK, but where's my chit-chat?

694
00:50:18,400 --> 00:50:20,901
[SPEAKER_03]: Include that in the experience of those two things.

695
00:50:22,201 --> 00:50:24,182
[SPEAKER_03]: Don't give into it and try to resolve it.

696
00:50:25,502 --> 00:50:28,243
[SPEAKER_03]: You're closer to resolution by not acting out of that craving.

697
00:50:29,527 --> 00:50:33,251
[SPEAKER_03]: But, of course, it was their very craving that brought you there.

698
00:50:34,532 --> 00:50:50,907
[SPEAKER_03]: If you didn't crave to see the citta, if you were not pressured towards it, if you did not generate a desire to do so, well, you would have not have... you would have not discerned the relationship between the internal physicality and feeling.

699
00:51:06,846 --> 00:51:12,450
[SPEAKER_03]: So, it's kind of like... you know how the aggregate of virtue sets up a fence around the wild animal?

700
00:51:13,611 --> 00:51:21,055
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, this is clearly like a... another sort of... layer to it.

701
00:51:22,657 --> 00:51:33,083
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you might not know, at times, where my mind is, or discern it peripherally correctly, but you know physicality and the feeling.

702
00:51:33,284 --> 00:51:35,065
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you know what has to be within that space.

703
00:51:36,816 --> 00:51:38,196
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why the space was relevant.

704
00:51:39,417 --> 00:51:40,697
[SPEAKER_03]: Cannot be outside of this.

705
00:51:41,137 --> 00:51:41,657
[SPEAKER_03]: Impossible.

706
00:51:41,878 --> 00:51:57,242
[SPEAKER_03]: In the same sense, well, I don't know where my moods come from, and what they are, and how they act, and how they pressure me, but I know they cannot pressure me on account of household life, they cannot pressure me on account of sensuality, ill-will, of this coarse nature in terms of the precepts.

707
00:51:57,782 --> 00:51:59,883
[SPEAKER_03]: They cannot, because those things have been abandoned.

708
00:52:14,526 --> 00:52:15,889
[SPEAKER_00]: Back to this physicality.

709
00:52:17,551 --> 00:52:24,703
[SPEAKER_00]: If you look at Majjhima 62, you see, like, the Buddha teaching Mahārūḍa.

710
00:52:26,165 --> 00:52:27,768
[SPEAKER_00]: And before he gets to ānāpānasati,

711
00:52:29,337 --> 00:52:33,159
[SPEAKER_00]: He's talking about the five aggregates are not yours.

712
00:52:33,459 --> 00:52:34,699
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's what you must see them as.

713
00:52:35,320 --> 00:52:41,702
[SPEAKER_00]: Then, he goes to the elements, but with specific bodily contemplation.

714
00:52:41,742 --> 00:52:56,508
[SPEAKER_00]: So, it's like whatever is internal, that is hard and solid, weight, gravity, and taken up, that is the earth element.

715
00:52:57,689 --> 00:52:57,829
[SPEAKER_00]: And

716
00:52:58,480 --> 00:52:59,921
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's like the hair of the head.

717
00:53:02,723 --> 00:53:04,404
[SPEAKER_00]: You have that... it gives you that idea.

718
00:53:04,604 --> 00:53:05,745
[SPEAKER_00]: Hair of the head, that thought.

719
00:53:06,306 --> 00:53:09,748
[SPEAKER_00]: Hair of the body, nails, teeth.

720
00:53:10,568 --> 00:53:19,895
[SPEAKER_00]: And it's like, to me, it's... you've got to find that internal, hard, solid, corresponding aspect.

721
00:53:20,515 --> 00:53:22,037
[SPEAKER_00]: You have an idea of hair of the head.

722
00:53:25,947 --> 00:53:28,168
[SPEAKER_00]: Where's the corresponding hardness of it?

723
00:53:28,288 --> 00:53:29,768
[SPEAKER_00]: Is that... Where's the hardness?

724
00:53:30,708 --> 00:53:32,969
[SPEAKER_00]: Where's the solidity of the weight of it?

725
00:53:34,589 --> 00:53:45,933
[SPEAKER_00]: Is it... You can't... You know, you can have the idea of the word and the concept... Yeah, what is the internal solidity of it?

726
00:53:46,313 --> 00:53:49,114
[SPEAKER_03]: Not external, because somebody could be touching the hair or something.

727
00:53:50,374 --> 00:53:50,974
[SPEAKER_03]: No, internally.

728
00:53:51,794 --> 00:53:53,635
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you want to include all those images

729
00:53:54,734 --> 00:54:03,997
[SPEAKER_03]: In that internal solidity... And why is that important?

730
00:54:05,458 --> 00:54:14,801
[SPEAKER_03]: Now, while we're talking about it... Why is it important to say... see all the five aggregates as not mine?

731
00:54:15,061 --> 00:54:21,724
[SPEAKER_03]: Or all the form, internal, external, earth, water, fire, air, to leave nothing out?

732
00:54:22,298 --> 00:54:23,078
[SPEAKER_03]: Why is that important?

733
00:54:23,098 --> 00:54:26,219
[SPEAKER_03]: To include it in that relationship of physicality, felt.

734
00:54:35,860 --> 00:54:39,461
[SPEAKER_04]: Whatever is left out is taken up as mind, isn't it?

735
00:54:40,641 --> 00:54:44,962
[SPEAKER_03]: But in terms of what we've been talking about, citta, why is it relevant for that?

736
00:54:46,342 --> 00:54:50,743
[SPEAKER_03]: Yes, of course, it's taken as mind, but in terms of this whole talk,

737
00:54:52,336 --> 00:54:53,756
[SPEAKER_03]: Why is it relevant to include everything?

738
00:54:54,176 --> 00:54:56,417
[SPEAKER_01]: Wait, to include it all within the relationship?

739
00:54:57,017 --> 00:54:57,177
[SPEAKER_01]: Or...

740
00:54:57,517 --> 00:54:57,737
[SPEAKER_00]: Yes.

741
00:54:58,317 --> 00:55:03,458
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, the relationship establishes, as I said, and then whatever is left out, you realize cannot be left out.

742
00:55:03,698 --> 00:55:10,779
[SPEAKER_03]: So, then, you are intentionally unleaving it out by bringing it up on the base of physicality felt.

743
00:55:12,299 --> 00:55:13,480
[SPEAKER_03]: Actually, that's a relationship, isn't it?

744
00:55:13,680 --> 00:55:14,640
[SPEAKER_03]: Physicality felt.

745
00:55:15,740 --> 00:55:19,121
[SPEAKER_03]: I don't need to say experience physicality in the field of healing.

746
00:55:19,921 --> 00:55:21,621
[SPEAKER_03]: Just physicality felt.

747
00:55:22,508 --> 00:55:23,389
[SPEAKER_03]: Both are already there.

748
00:55:25,370 --> 00:55:32,394
[SPEAKER_03]: So, why is it important to include things that were tacitly excluded?

749
00:55:33,255 --> 00:55:33,915
[SPEAKER_01]: What is that?

750
00:55:35,116 --> 00:55:37,017
[SPEAKER_01]: Is it that that's important?

751
00:55:37,398 --> 00:55:42,781
[SPEAKER_01]: Or just kind of if things are left out, then you're not seeing either end properly?

752
00:55:44,923 --> 00:55:47,024
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, so to speak, like... That is important.

753
00:55:51,802 --> 00:55:54,063
[SPEAKER_01]: But, I guess, this is...

754
00:55:54,723 --> 00:55:59,346
[SPEAKER_03]: So, you are seeing, say, you are factually experiencing physicality, feeling felt.

755
00:56:01,046 --> 00:56:07,569
[SPEAKER_03]: But, the Sutra encourages to start including all these seemingly less relevant things.

756
00:56:09,390 --> 00:56:13,752
[SPEAKER_03]: Oh, internal bile and bones and this... Why?

757
00:56:15,113 --> 00:56:16,914
[SPEAKER_04]: Well, to disassociate those things.

758
00:56:17,194 --> 00:56:17,594
[SPEAKER_03]: From what?

759
00:56:17,674 --> 00:56:19,355
[SPEAKER_04]: From the internal physicality.

760
00:56:23,289 --> 00:56:23,689
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, no.

761
00:56:23,729 --> 00:56:26,212
[SPEAKER_03]: You are kind of associating with internal physicality.

762
00:56:27,493 --> 00:56:28,233
[SPEAKER_00]: First, at least.

763
00:56:28,514 --> 00:56:29,154
[SPEAKER_00]: That's what you're doing.

764
00:56:30,295 --> 00:56:32,397
[SPEAKER_03]: They are disassociated from physicality internally.

765
00:56:32,417 --> 00:56:33,238
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why they're left out.

766
00:56:34,739 --> 00:56:39,003
[SPEAKER_03]: When you think internal physicality, you don't have the images of your bones and marrow and stuff.

767
00:56:40,904 --> 00:56:42,205
[SPEAKER_02]: You haven't associated them with it.

768
00:56:43,947 --> 00:56:44,087
[SPEAKER_04]: Okay.

769
00:56:44,167 --> 00:56:45,708
[SPEAKER_04]: I'm going from the other direction.

770
00:56:47,590 --> 00:56:49,792
[SPEAKER_03]: So, in the context of what we've been talking about,

771
00:56:50,450 --> 00:57:06,875
[SPEAKER_00]: Mind, citta, the animal, why is it important to include all these images, all these things, all these implicit... Why is it important to include the image with the physicality, essentially?

772
00:57:07,075 --> 00:57:08,796
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, like what you were describing.

773
00:57:08,836 --> 00:57:15,478
[SPEAKER_03]: Like, oh, any... okay, internally... body experienced internally and starts including

774
00:57:16,037 --> 00:57:20,138
[SPEAKER_03]: The hair, the nails, the extent of all of that internally.

775
00:57:20,198 --> 00:57:21,298
[SPEAKER_03]: Why is that relevant?

776
00:57:21,478 --> 00:57:22,319
[SPEAKER_02]: It's peaceful.

777
00:57:22,439 --> 00:57:23,279
[SPEAKER_03]: Well, let's say like this.

778
00:57:23,739 --> 00:57:27,980
[SPEAKER_03]: No, again, that doesn't bear any answer to citta that I'm asking.

779
00:57:29,040 --> 00:57:32,181
[SPEAKER_03]: So, what happens to citta if you're not including it?

